  "rationale": [
    "Uniform TC+stock has two important hard-role dual-endpoint improvements over both inherited BASE and stock: K35 and RB35-T2. This is enough complete-method signal to justify a limited continuation, rather than closing solely because every role does not win.",
    "K15 and K20 retain their qualified certificates, including the K20 benefit relative to the open stable baseline, but both are slower than stock and TC2. These adverse certified-time comparisons must remain explicit.",
    "RX35-T2 improves verified U but weakens supported L relative to both BASE and stock. TC2 is better than old TC in both endpoints on this role. The old-TC candidate therefore has an observed mixed boundary, not full dominance.",
    "The T1 variants of the same RB35/RX35 base inputs directly test whether this hard-role behavior persists at shorter physical horizons. RX20 supplies the remaining different base input, including the historical root where old TC had no objective increment.",
    "The planned three positions complete only one uniform follow-up candidate. TC2 remains a five-role complete comparison with valid mathematical and same-domain LP increments; TC+stock results are explicitly the landing of an existing combination and are not attributed to TC2."
  ],
